"semdrift_exp_drift_001028","sympy","04a7da3aacdf095556c451cd17f3f33bf241a5f2","sympy/physics/vector/frame.py","set_ang_vel","def set_ang_vel(self, otherframe, value):
        """"""Define the angular velocity vector in a ReferenceFrame.

        Defines the angular velocity of this ReferenceFrame, in another.
        Angular velocity can be defined with respect to multiple different
        ReferenceFrames. Care must be taken to not create loops which are
        inconsistent.

        Parameters
        ==========

        otherframe : ReferenceFrame
            A ReferenceFrame to define the angular velocity in
        value : Vector
            The Vector representing angular velocity

        Examples
        ========

        >>> from sympy.physics.vector import ReferenceFrame
        >>> N = ReferenceFrame('N')
        >>> A = ReferenceFrame('A')
        >>> V = 10 * N.x
        >>> A.set_ang_vel(N, V)
        >>> A.ang_vel_in(N)
        10*N.x

        """"""

        if value == 0:
            value = Vector(0)
        value = _check_vector(value)
        _check_frame(otherframe)
        self._ang_vel_dict.update({otherframe: value})
        otherframe._ang_vel_dict.update({self: -value})","Define the angular velocity vector in a ReferenceFrame.

Defines the angular velocity of this ReferenceFrame, in another.
Angular velocity can be defined with respect to multiple different
ReferenceFrames. Care must be taken to not create loops which are
inconsistent.

Parameters
==========

otherframe : ReferenceFrame
    A ReferenceFrame to define the angular velocity in
value : Vector
    The Vector representing angular velocity

Examples
========

>>> from sympy.physics.vector import ReferenceFrame
>>> N = ReferenceFrame('N')
>>> A = ReferenceFrame('A')
>>> V = 10 * N.x
>>> A.set_ang_vel(N, V)
>>> A.ang_vel_in(N)
10*N.x

