But any number of enum mixins can appear in a class definition
(even if multiple enum bases define __new__). So this is fine:

    class Foo(enum.Enum):
        def __new__(cls, val): ...
    class Bar(enum.Enum):
        def __new__(cls, val): ...
    class Baz(int, Foo, Bar, enum.Flag): ...

