       <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confusion_matrix>`_
       (Wikipedia and other references may use a different
       convention for axes).

Examples
--------
>>> from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix
>>> y_pred = [0, 0, 2, 2, 0, 2]
array([[2, 0, 0],
       [0, 0, 1],
       [1, 0, 2]])

>>> y_pred = [""ant"", ""ant"", ""cat"", ""cat"", ""ant"", ""cat""]
