"semdrift_exp_drift_000332","sympy","04a7da3aacdf095556c451cd17f3f33bf241a5f2","sympy/ntheory/ecm.py","mont_ladder","def mont_ladder(self, k):
        """"""
        Scalar multiplication of a point in Montgomery form
        using Montgomery Ladder Algorithm.
        A total of 11 multiplications are required in each step of this
        algorithm.

        Parameters
        ==========

        k : The positive integer multiplier

        Examples
        ========

        >>> from sympy.ntheory.ecm import Point
        >>> p1 = Point(11, 16, 7, 29)
        >>> p3 = p1.mont_ladder(3)
        >>> p3.x_cord
        23
        >>> p3.z_cord
        17
        """"""
        Q = self
        R = self.double()
        for i in bin(k)[3:]:
            if  i  == '1':
                Q = R.add(Q, self)
                R = R.double()
            else:
                R = Q.add(R, self)
                Q = Q.double()
        return Q","Scalar multiplication of a point in Montgomery form
using Montgomery Ladder Algorithm.
A total of 11 multiplications are required in each step of this
algorithm.

Parameters
==========

k : The positive integer multiplier

