Y_val : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples_Y, n_features),             default=None
    Matrix `Y_val`.

Returns
-------
distances : ndarray of shape (n_samples_X, n_samples_Y)
    Returns the cosine distance between samples in X and Y_val.

See Also
--------
cosine_similarity : Compute cosine similarity between samples in X and Y_val.
scipy.spatial.distance.cosine : Dense matrices only.

Examples
--------
>>> from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_distances
>>> X = [[0, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1]]
>>> Y_val = [[1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 0]]
>>> cosine_distances(X, Y_val)
array([[1.   , 1.   ],
       [0.422, 0.183]])","1","parameter_rename","Parameter 'Y' in code signature is documented under stale identifier 'Y_val'.","train"
