"semdrift_exp_drift_001469","scipy","e6fa3531f47123a5008fe0909d00256c161b66e9","scipy/interpolate/_polyint.py","approximate_taylor_polynomial","def approximate_taylor_polynomial(f,x,degree,scale,order=None):
    """"""
    Estimate the Taylor polynomial of f at x by polynomial fitting.

    .. deprecated:: 1.18.0
        This function is deprecated and will be removed in SciPy 2.1.0. Use the
        following code instead:

        .. code-block:: python

            import numpy as np

            def f(z): return np.exp(z**2)  # example function
            N = 10  # number of terms in the Taylor expansion
            zz = np.exp(2j * np.pi * np.arange(N) / N)  # roots of unity
            c = np.fft.fft(f(zz)) / N
            c = np.real(c)  # c must be real by symmetry


    Parameters
