n : positive int
    Must be strictly greater than zero.","1","parameter_constraint_mismatch","Docstring specifies strict positive integer constraint on 'n', while code implementation accepts arbitrary inputs without positive validation.","train"
"semdrift_exp_drift_000948","sympy","04a7da3aacdf095556c451cd17f3f33bf241a5f2","sympy/assumptions/handlers/sets.py","_","def _(expr, assumptions):
    """"""
    * Hermitian**Integer  -> !Antihermitian
    * Antihermitian**Even -> !Antihermitian
    * Antihermitian**Odd  -> Antihermitian
    """"""
    if expr.is_number:
        raise MDNotImplementedError
    if _ask_recursive(Q.hermitian(expr.base), assumptions):
        if _ask_recursive(Q.integer(expr.exp), assumptions):
            return False
    elif _ask_recursive(Q.antihermitian(expr.base), assumptions):
        if _ask_recursive(Q.even(expr.exp), assumptions):
            return False
        elif _ask_recursive(Q.odd(expr.exp), assumptions):
            return True
    raise MDNotImplementedError","* Hermitian**Integer  -> !Antihermitian
* Antihermitian**Even -> !Antihermitian
* Antihermitian**Odd  -> Antihermitian

