"semdrift_exp_drift_001033","sympy","04a7da3aacdf095556c451cd17f3f33bf241a5f2","sympy/core/intfunc.py","num_digits","def num_digits(n, base=10):
    """"""Return the number of digits needed to express n in give base.

    Examples
    ========

    >>> from sympy.core.intfunc import num_digits
    >>> num_digits(10)
    2
    >>> num_digits(10, 2)  # 1010 -> 4 digits
    4
    >>> num_digits(-100, 16)  # -64 -> 2 digits
    2


    Parameters
    ==========

    n: integer
        The number whose digits are counted.

    b: integer
        The base in which digits are computed.

    See Also
    ========
    sympy.ntheory.digits.digits, sympy.ntheory.digits.count_digits
    """"""
    if base < 0:
        raise ValueError('base must be int greater than 1')
    if not n:
        return 1
    e, t = integer_log(abs(n), base)
    return 1 + e","Return the number of digits needed to express n in give base.

Examples
========

>>> from sympy.core.intfunc import num_digits
>>> num_digits(10)
2
>>> num_digits(10, 2)  # 1010 -> 4 digits
4
>>> num_digits(-100, 16)  # -64 -> 2 digits
2


Parameters
==========

n: integer
    The number whose digits are counted.

b: integer
    The base in which digits are computed.

See Also
========
sympy.ntheory.digits.digits, sympy.ntheory.digits.count_digits

